{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true},{"text":" is a destination that posts each batch it receives as one request. The body is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever its ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"text":" writes for the batch’s records, so events need no ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conformance and the wire format is yours. It sends with ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","isActive":true},{"text":" by default, or through any ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","isActive":true},{"text":" you pass.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A send that gets no response, or a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, is sent again after the next wait of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff"},{"type":"text","text":": 1 second, doubling up to 60 seconds, unless you pass another. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination takes the next batch only once this one is delivered or dropped, so a tracker’s store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps the batch’s records until then. A batch the endpoint answers with any other status, whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request can never be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped, logged and reported on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":" as an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracing instrument injects the trace context of the batch’s first record into the request’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"header fields, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reach for this module to send to a server whose format you write yourself. For TraffluentCollector’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format, give the destination a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"text":"); for PostHog, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogBatchEncoder"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"text":"). To read events inside the app or in a test, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destinations"},{"text":") instead.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","","struct PlansEncoder: BatchEncoder {","    func encode(_ batch: [EventRecord]) -> EncodedBatch {","        let plans = batch.compactMap { ($0.event as? SignedUp)?.plan }","        return EncodedBatch(body: Data(plans.joined(separator: \"\\n\").utf8), contentType: \"text\/plain\")","    }","}","","let server = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: endpointURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder(),","    backoff: try ExponentialBackoff(initialDelay: .seconds(2), maximumDelay: .seconds(120)))","let drops = server.dropReports","let watching = Task {","    for await drop in drops {","        print(\"Dropped a batch: \\(drop)\")","    }","}","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: server)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers this destination beside the others, and what a delivery does while a batch is retried."}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"],"anchor":"Sending-batches","title":"Sending batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch"],"anchor":"Encoding-a-batch","title":"Encoding a batch"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/NonPositiveRetry"],"anchor":"Waiting-between-attempts","title":"Waiting between attempts"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError"],"anchor":"Sending-requests","title":"Sending requests"}],"metadata